WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:13.500
Hi, this is Dr. Jelena Trajkovic from CECS Department, Cal State Long Beach. This is a summary of everything that we learned today.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:29.500
This is a very good resource for you to make by yourself and to understand that there is a process when we need to convert numbers.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.540
so we're going to start from

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:32.740
converting

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.100
binary to decimal

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.320
number as you see here

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:45.080
in case we have a binary number in format B

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.720
with most significant bit

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.100
Bn-1

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.300
then Bn-2

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.860
to B0

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.940
the first thing that we need to ask

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.340
ourselves is

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.660
what is its representation?

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:05.500
Is it unsigned or is it signed?

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.100
So for unsigned representation,

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.940
please do remember that these are positive numbers only.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.500
And only thing that we need to do

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.340
is multiply each coefficient

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.060
with corresponding two to the power of

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.980
corresponding index.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:31.100
You get value of decimal number,

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.820
and you're done. Nothing else needs to be done.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.580
So this is the first thing that we have learned when we started talking about binary numbers.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:47.780
However, if the representation is signed, you have to ask further questions.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:57.140
Further question is, is the representation signed magnitude or the representation is

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:09.860
to complement. If we are in sine magnitude representation, what we need to do is we need

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:18.900
to basically partition our number. We literally take snips with scissors and look at b and

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:29.900
n-1. That one is going to determine the sign. And then we stick the remaining bits, so bn-2

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:38.940
to be zero, and we use the same procedure that we use here, which is annotated with two

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:47.140
stars here, to get the absolute value. The third step is that we combine. We take the

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:52.920
sign that we got in step one we take the absolute value that we got in step two

00:02:52.920 --> 00:03:05.500
and we are done. Now if we have number that is signed and that it's in tooth

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:11.380
complement we have to ask further questions. First question that we are

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:19.020
going to ask is number positive or negative? We are going to determine this

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:29.020
by observing the most significant fit for bn-1. If bn-1 is 0, then the number is positive,

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:38.020
and we continue in this round. If bn-1 is 1, we continue on the right-hand side of the chart.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:46.020
If the number is positive, we are just going to follow the same procedure, annotate it here, and we are done.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:50.020
There is nothing else that we can do. We have to do that.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:04:03.020
However, if the number is bn-1 is 1, that signifies the number is negative, then we need to find its two complements.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:14.020
Flip the bits, add one. Once we add one, we again have to come back to the procedure shown here,

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.020
and to get absolute value.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:19.360
Because we know that number is negative

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.780
this is basically

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.300
step 0.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:32.240
We will be combining here. We will be combining here step 0

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.200
and we will be combining

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.200
step 3

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:41.200
and we are going to get the whole value of the number and the f1.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.400
So this was

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:56.760
from binary to decimal. Let's look in the other way around. What happens if we are converting

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:07.280
from decimal to binary? First question that we need to ask is how many bits do we have

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:16.070
use sometimes number of bits is given to you but sometimes that number is is not

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:23.870
given and you have to figure out by yourself so if you need in both cases

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:29.470
you're going to go with procedure as shown below and you are going to ask

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:42.150
yourself is the number of bits that you allocated sufficient or not. Okay again

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:48.590
second question that we ask is the representation that we are having. So are

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:57.790
we using unsigned or we are using signed numbers? If we are using unsigned numbers

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:02.790
Again, remind yourself that these are only positive numbers.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:06.790
What we need to take is the number itself.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:09.790
Keep dividing by 2.

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:14.790
Keep noting both the integer part and remainder.

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:23.790
Read from the bottom up and we have the number itself.

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:31.630
We can add leading zeros. If we have enough space, if someone tells me,

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:38.990
hey, you know, please tell, give me six bits representation of number 10, sure,

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:48.030
you can add leading zeros to it to make it six bits. You do not, for unsigned numbers,

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:56.150
you do not have to because in unsigned numbers most significant bit is not

00:06:56.150 --> 00:07:02.070
special in any case. It is one of the bits that is giving you the absolute

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:09.690
value of the number. If you ask the question what kind of representation do

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:18.420
you either want and you got the requirement for signed you have to ask

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:24.540
yourself do you want sine magnitude or tooth complement? If it is sine magnitude

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:32.460
representation you are going to designate one bit for a place for one bit

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:36.960
that is going to carry your sine bit and depending of what number you have

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:46.080
positive or negative you're going to insert zero or one. For the remaining bits

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:51.880
that are providing your absolute value, you're going to keep using the same

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:57.240
procedure and outline on the far left of this chart. You're going to put those

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:07.970
two pieces together and you're done. If we are using signed numbers, those

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:16.190
complement, we will again have to figure out if the number that we have to

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:23.630
convert from decimal to binary is a positive number or negative number. If the

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:31.110
number is positive we are going to follow the procedure outlined here and

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:49.070
please make sure that you have enough space so that the leading or MSB

00:08:49.070 --> 00:09:09.900
leading bit for MSB stays 0. If the decimal number is negative, what you are going to

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:15.940
do is take the absolute value of this decimal number. With this absolute value of this decimal

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:21.460
number you are going to follow the same procedure as outlined here and you are going to make

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:24.260
and bit number.

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:25.560
Watch out.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:32.900
This one has to start with

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.360
leading

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:39.660
no significant bit.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:43.520
Then you are going to flip all the bits, add one

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:46.020
and you are going to be one.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.860
I hope this was helpful. Thank you for watching.

